, and a history that goes back generations.\nIt also has ghosts.\n\nJoin me for a **90-minute evening walking tour through Cabbagetown**, where we'll explore some of the neighbourhood's strangest stories, unsettling legends, and darker pieces of Toronto's past.\n\nWe'll begin beneath the glass of **Allan Gardens**, then make our way through the streets of Cabbagetown, stopping along the way for stories of mysterious creatures, haunted buildings, old prisons, cemeteries, restless spirits, and the people who may never have quite left.\nThis isn't a traditional history walk.\n\nIt's a **ghost tour** — so expect some history, some local legends, a little mystery, and a few stories that are difficult to explain.\nAnd, of course, we'll have a few laughs along the way.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 👻 What We'll Explore\n\nOur route will take us through some of Cabbagetown's most atmospheric locations, including:\n🌿 **Allan Gardens** — ghosts beneath the glass\n🐾 **Winchester Square Park** — the strange story of Cabbagetown's Tunnel Monster\n🍸 **The Winchester Hotel** — spirits that may have never checked out\n🏚️ **Winchester Street** — haunted houses and Victorian secrets\n⛓️ **The Don Jail \u0026 Bridgepoint** — where the walls remember everything\n🐄 **Riverdale Farm** — and its strange connection to the old Don Jail\n⚰️ **The Toronto Necropolis** — a city of the dead beneath a city of the living\n🕯️ **St. James Town \u0026 St. James' Cemetery** — where the living and the dead share the same neighbourhood\nAnd much, much more...\n\n***\n\n## 🌙 What Makes This Tour Different?\n\nThis is a **new ghost walk for the group**, created specifically around Cabbagetown.\nRather than simply walking from one location to another, the route has been **curated around the stories** so that each stop connects to the next.\n\nWe'll move through the neighbourhood at a comfortable pace, stopping along the way while I share the stories behind the places we're visiting.\nSome stories are historical.\nSome are local legends.\nSome are downright strange.\nYou'll have to decide for yourself which ones you believe. 👻\n\n***\n\n## 🕯️ A Little About the Tour\n\nThis is a **90-minute evening walk**.\nWe will be walking outdoors throughout the tour and will **not be entering buildings**.\nSome locations may be viewed from outside or from nearby public spaces.\nPlease be respectful of residents, private property, and cemetery grounds as we make our way through the neighbourhood.\n\n***\n\n## 📍 Meetup Details\n\n🕚 **Meeting Time:** 6:30 PM\nI will only wait **5 minutes** before we begin.\n🫎 **Meeting Location:** Outside the **Palm House at Allan Gardens (this BIG WHITE building)**\nLook for me in my **Moose Hat!**\n🏁 **End Point:** Parliament Street \u0026 Wellesley Street East\n🚶 **Walking Time:** Approximately 90 minutes\n👻 **Pace:** Comfortable, steady walking pace\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$10 cash or e-transfer**\n📧 **[mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)**\nThe $10 fee helps support the group and covers the **extra research, preparation, and curation that goes into creating these ghost walks**.\nThese aren't simply walks where we meet up and wander around.\nI've put together a specific route, researched the stories, and created a series of stops designed to turn the walk into an actual **storytelling experience**.\nYou're paying for the experience — not just the walking.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🧥 Weather-appropriate clothing\n💧 Water\n🔦 A little extra light if you have it\n👻 An open mind\nAnd maybe don't wander off by yourself.\nYou never know who's walking behind you.\n\n***\n\n## ⚠️ A Quick Note\n\nSometimes things happen and I may need to cancel or change an event.\nPlease keep an eye on the event page for updates.\nYou can RSVP ahead of time — or **just show up on the day if you're not sure about your schedule.**\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis walk is for anyone who enjoys:\n👻 Ghost stories and local legends\n🏙️ Toronto history\n🚶 Social walking\n📸 Exploring different neighbourhoods\n🕯️ Strange and unusual stories\n😂 A good story without taking ourselves too seriously\nYou don't have to be a believer.\nYou don't even have to be scared.\nJust come for the walk and see what you think.\n\n###\n\n**Organizer:** Mathew\n📧 **[torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com)**\n\n### **👋 Come for the stories.**\n\n### **🚶 Stay for the walk.**\n\n### **👻 And keep an eye out for who might be walking with us.**","eventType":"PHYSICAL","eventUrl":"https://www.meetup.com/no-such-thing-as-bad-weather/events/316201312/","isAttending":false,"isSaved":false,"maxTickets":0,"rsvpState":"JOIN_OPEN","featuredEventPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:535755486"},"displayPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:535755486"},"feeSettings":{"__typename":"EventFeeSettings","accepts":"CASH","currency":"CAD","amount":10},"group":{"__ref":"Group:35508019"},"socialProofInsights":{"__typename":"SocialProofInsights","isTrendingEvent":false,"totalInterestedUsers":30,"interestedUsersSample":[{"__typename":"Member","memberPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:274445427"}},{"__typename":"Member","memberPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:301409506"}},{"__typename":"Member","memberPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:139232652"}},{"__typename":"Member","memberPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:262876286"}},{"__typename":"Member","memberPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:275142716"}},{"__typename":"Member","memberPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:305779113"}},{"__typename":"Member","memberPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:269205848"}}]},"rsvps":{"__typename":"RsvpConnection","totalCount":1,"edges":[{"__typename":"RsvpEdge","node":{"__typename":"Rsvp","isHost":true,"member":{"__ref":"Member:9334356"}}}]},"series":null,"venue":{"__typename":"Venue","name":"Allen Gardens Conservatory","address":"19 Horticultural Ave","city":"Toronto","